```json
{
  "pcr_probability": 0.65,
  "conclusion": "likely_pcr",
  "evidence": [
    {"feature": "HER2", "value": 1, "direction": "supports_pcr"},
    {"feature": "HR", "value": 1, "direction": "against_pcr"},
    {"feature": "age", "value": 32, "direction": "supports_pcr"},
    {"feature": "MammaPrint", "value": 0, "direction": "neutral"}
  ],
  "report": "This patient has a favorable profile for achieving pCR with neoadjuvant therapy. The HER2-positive status is the strongest predictor of excellent response to HER2-targeted regimens. Young age further supports a higher likelihood of response. While HR positivity modestly lowers the expected pCR probability compared to pure HER2-positive/HR-negative disease, the overall prognosis remains highly favorable. The low-risk MammaPrint category suggests a tumor biology that may be more responsive to therapy. Overall, this patient is a strong candidate for achieving a complete pathologic response."
}
```

