  "pcr_probability": 0.08,
  "conclusion": "unlikely_pcr",
  "evidence": [
    {"feature": "HR", "value": 1, "direction": "against_pcr"},
    {"feature": "HER2", "value": 0, "direction": "against_pcr"},
    {"feature": "TNBC", "value": 0, "direction": "against_pcr"},
    {"feature": "MammaPrint", "value": 0, "direction": "neutral"}
  ],
  "report": "This patient has hormone receptor-positive, HER2-negative breast cancer (luminal subtype), which is associated with a low likelihood of pathologic complete response to neoadjuvant chemotherapy. The absence of high-risk genomic classification by MammaPrint does not substantially alter this baseline expectation. Age is not a major independent predictor of pCR in this context. Overall, the tumor biology suggests a lower probability of achieving pCR compared to HER2-positive or triple-negative subtypes."
}
```

