    {"feature": "HER2", "value": 0, "direction": "against_pcr"},
    {"feature": "MammaPrint", "value": 1, "direction": "supports_pcr"},
    {"feature": "age", "value": 53, "direction": "neutral"}
  ],
  "report": "This patient has hormone receptor-positive (HR+), HER2-negative breast cancer with a high-risk MammaPrint result. HR+/HER2- tumors generally have lower pCR rates compared to HER2-positive or triple-negative subtypes, as they are typically less chemosensitive. While the high-risk genomic profile indicates a more aggressive tumor biology that may respond better to chemotherapy than low-risk HR+ disease, the overall probability of achieving a pathologic complete response remains relatively low in this biomarker subset. The patient should be counseled that while neoadjuvant therapy is beneficial for prognostic information and surgical planning, the likelihood of eradicating all invasive cancer is modest."
}
```

